    60	\noindent
    61	Using  this threshold rank, we earlier defined the corresponding eigenvectors as \textit{threshold rank eigenvectors}.
    62	We recall that our main idea is to show that the dual variables $B_{ij}$'s can be chosen such that a $\tau$-\textit{threshold rank eigenvector} $\mathbf{v}^{\paren{l}}$ with eigenvalue $\lambda_l$ of $\restrict{A}{S \times S}$ can be extended (by padding it with $0's$) to be the eigenvector\footnote{With slight abuse of notation we will call these padded vectors of length $n$ also as $\mathbf{v}^{\paren{l}}$.} of the dual matrix $Y$ with eigenvalue $d+\lambda_l$. For this to hold true we additionally require (in addition to the constraints (1)-(4) in \prettyref{sec:traditional_sdp}), that we have,
