| G6 | pass | five attacks each 0/8; Gaussian reference 8/8; compact formula 8/8 |
| G7 | pass | doubled `n=64` built in 0.000505 s and verified; answer-space bits grew 992 to 1,984 |
| G8 | pass | 140/140 invariant relabellings, 140/140 carried witnesses valid, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
| G9 | pass | structural-hint verdict hardened; 334 actual answer chars, 353 worst-case, 32 elements, 226 intended operations |

The G6 attacks were public-key magnitude/rank as an outlier statistic, greedy left-to-right zero fill, the diagonal-only relaxation, eight small scalar guesses after noticing rank one, and 256 uniform random restarts.  Each failed on all eight audited seeds.

