We defer proving the existence of such <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>’s to <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Setting dual variables using Farkas’ Lemma ‣ 2 Exact recovery in polynomial time using SDP ‣ Exact recovery algorithm for Planted Bipartite Graph in Semi-random Graphs" class="ltx_ref">Section <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></span></a>. However since the equation <a href="#S2.E26" title="In 2.1 Constructing an optimal dual ‣ 2 Exact recovery in polynomial time using SDP ‣ Exact recovery algorithm for Planted Bipartite Graph in Semi-random Graphs" class="ltx_ref">(<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></span>)</a> only concerns <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{ij}\in S\times\left(V\setminus S\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{ij}\in S\times\left(V\setminus S\right)</annotation></semantics></math> we can set <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{ij}=0,\forall\left\{i,j\right\}\in\left(V\setminus S\times V\setminus S\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{ij}=0,\forall\left\{i,j\right\}\in\left(V\setminus S\times V\setminus S\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since equation <a href="#S1.E9" title="In Characterizing dual variables through optimality conditions: ‣ 1.4.2 Traditional SDP Analysis ‣ 1.4 Proof Overview ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Exact recovery algorithm for Planted Bipartite Graph in Semi-random Graphs" class="ltx_ref">(<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></span>)</a> already forces us to set <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{ij}\in S\times S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{ij}\in S\times S</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> we have,</p>
