<div id="Thmtheorem22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
Lemma 22
<div id="Thmtheorem22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,k,d,p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,k,d,p</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}\left(A_{\left(V\setminus S\right)\times\left(V\setminus S\right)}-p\mathbbm{1}_{V\setminus S}\mathbbm{1}_{V\setminus S}^{T}\right)\geqslant-\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}\left(A_{\left(V\setminus S\right)\times\left(V\setminus S\right)}-p\mathbbm{1}_{V\setminus S}\mathbbm{1}_{V\setminus S}^{T}\right)\geqslant-\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant\left(512/\alpha p^{7/2}\right)\sqrt{n\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>512</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant\left(512/\alpha p^{7/2}\right)\sqrt{n\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\geqslant 1/2+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\geqslant 1/2+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and for choice of <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\left(d\left(1/2-\alpha\right)/\left(1/2+\alpha\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\left(d\left(1/2-\alpha\right)/\left(1/2+\alpha\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geqslant 5\left(\left(\log k\right)/\gamma^{4}k\right)^{1/6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geqslant 5\left(\left(\log k\right)/\gamma^{4}k\right)^{1/6}</annotation></semantics></math> and if there exists a <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying equation <a href="#S2.E26" title="In 2.1 Constructing an optimal dual ‣ 2 Exact recovery in polynomial time using SDP ‣ Exact recovery algorithm for Planted Bipartite Graph in Semi-random Graphs" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_upright">(<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></span>)</a> such that <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert B\right\rVert\leqslant 896\sqrt{n\left(\log k\right)}/p^{5/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>896</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert B\right\rVert\leqslant 896\sqrt{n\left(\log k\right)}/p^{5/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, with high probability (over the randomness of the input) the dual matrix <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
--
